    {
      "id": "claim_51d80a1112b74af3af85b5b6cb66d91a",
      "statement": "scripts/publish-wiki.mjs is dependency-free (Node built-ins only), letting the Publish Wiki workflow skip npm ci; it walks openwiki/ (skipping dotfiles and index.md), derives each wiki page's flat name from the source file PATH rather than the front-matter title (e.g. engine/eval-harness.md -> Engine-Eval-Harness) so a retitled page keeps a stable URL, rewrites internal markdown links to the corresponding wiki page names, and removes pre-existing top-level *.md files in the wiki checkout before rendering so deleted source pages don't linger as orphans.",
